/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\n31\t+internal/roles/     starter role directories embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\n32\t internal/pool/      slot arbiter for max_pods (stdlib only, no I/O): priority classes, per-issue triage cap\n33\t internal/effects/   the only writer: Effects interface, Live and DryRun (JSONL ledger), Open factory; archtest/ enforces \"only effects writes\"\n34\t internal/gitx/      git CLI wrapper (Commit, Push, StagedPaths, FileAt); gittest/ builds bare-repo fixtures; Commit/Push are for internal/effects only\n35\tdiff --git a/docs/proposal.md b/docs/proposal.md\n36\tindex e3e8925..c6d63fe 100644\n37\t--- a/docs/proposal.md\n38\t+++ b/docs/proposal.md\n39\t@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@ A scanner is a directory, `.ard/scanners/<name>/`, holding either an executable\n40\t | lts | endoflife.date + manifests: go.mod, package.json, Dockerfile `FROM`, Helm charts | 7 d | 1 per component | yes |\n41\t | lint | repo linters, findings beyond a committed baseline | 24 h | 20 per rule and directory | yes |\n42\t | error-codes | pattern match over source, registry and docs files (`sh` + `jq`) | 24 h | 20 | yes |\n43\t+| trufflehog | leaked-credential scan of the current commit (`sh` + `jq` + TruffleHog) | 24 h | 1 | yes |\n44\t | missing-tests | coverage report plus exported functions with no test | 24 h | 10 per package | yes |\n45\t | docs | undocumented exported Go identifiers and package comments (deterministic) | 3 d | 10 per package | yes |\n46\t | docs-drift | LLM: docs that contradict the code (planned; needs the LLM scanner engine, #204) | 3 d | 10 per doc file | no |\n47\t@@ -219,6 +220,8 @@ A scanner is a directory, `.ard/scanners/<name>/`, holding either an executable\n48\t \n49\t **The error-codes scanner** (`scanners/error-codes`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program, pattern match over source, registry and docs files) reads a human-owned `codes.json` in its role directory; nothing ships one, because error-code conventions are specific to each repository. Keys: `pattern` (required, a regex of at most 512 characters, wrapped so `E1001` does not match inside `XE10011`; it must not match the empty string), `registry` (required, a list of path patterns), `entry` (optional: a registry line must also match it to define a code), `docs` (optional; unset turns the undocumented check off), `sources` (optional, default every text file) and `exclude`. A path pattern ending in `/` is a directory prefix from the root, one without `/` matches the base name, and any other is a glob on the whole path (`*` and `?` stop at `/`, `**` does not). Unknown keys, wrong types and lists over 100 entries are errors. Codes found in registry files (on `entry` lines) are R, codes anywhere in docs files are D, codes in every other text file are S. Findings: `error-codes:duplicated:<code>` (high, group `duplicate codes`: a code on two or more distinct registry lines), `error-codes:unregistered:<code>` (medium, group `unregistered codes`: in S, not in R) and `error-codes:undocumented:<code>` (low, group `undocumented codes`: in R, not in D, only when `docs` is set). Fingerprints use the code alone, so moving a use never churns an issue. `.git`, `.ard`, `vendor`, `node_modules`, `testdata`, symlinks, binary files, files of about 1 MiB or more and lines over 16 KiB are skipped. A finding carries only the code and repo-relative `path:line` locations, never line text, and codes outside `[A-Za-z0-9_.:/+=-]{1,128}` are dropped with a stderr count. Because the scanner is `autoclose`, it fails the run rather than see less: an invalid `codes.json`, a `registry` or `docs` that matches no file, a file in both, an unreadable file, a failing tool or more than 5,000 findings all exit non-zero with no output. With no `codes.json` it logs `not configured` and succeeds with no findings, so deleting `codes.json` closes its open issues as \"No longer detected\". ard does not run it on itself until ard has error codes.\n50\t \n51\t+**The trufflehog scanner** (`scanners/trufflehog`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program) runs `trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2` on the current commit. It never verifies a credential against a provider. Only the detector name, file, line and a hash of the secret leave the scan: `Raw`, `RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData` and `StructuredData` stay in pipes inside `scan`. The fingerprint is `trufflehog:` plus the first 16 hex digits of SHA-256 over `ard-trufflehog-v1`, a NUL byte and the base64 of the secret (an unsalted hash, so one value gives one issue wherever it appears). The scan fails closed: a non-zero trufflehog exit, a missing `finished scanning` summary, zero chunks on a non-empty tree, or a result count that differs from the summary produces no findings, so nothing is autoclosed on a partial run. `exclude-paths` (regexes; `.git` is always excluded) and `allow` (one fingerprint per line) are human-owned; a bad `allow` entry fails the run. Findings use `route: needs-human`, severity high, and carry a runbook that says to rotate the credential first. `commit` is the scanned SHA, recorded in `.ard/<n>/issue.md`; history is not scanned. TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0: it is installed by the role's Dockerfile and is not in the published `ard` image.\n52\t+\n53\t **The docs scanner** (`scanners/docs`, a `sh` script plus one stdlib-only Go program, `docscan.go`, built at scan time with the job's own Go) lists undocumented exported Go identifiers. It reports, per package directory: a missing package comment; an exported function, a method on an exported receiver type (pointer, value or generic) and an exported type with no doc comment (the spec's doc, its trailing comment or the enclosing declaration's doc all count); and an exported const or var with no comment, one finding per parenthesised block that has no block comment. Struct fields, interface methods, methods on unexported types and comment wording are not checked. Every exported identifier counts, `internal/` included, and files for every platform count (build constraints are not evaluated). It skips `testdata/`, `vendor/`, `node_modules/` and dot or underscore directories, files whose names start with `_` or `.`, symlinks, `*_test.go`, `//go:build ignore` files, generated files and `package main`. The fingerprint is `docs:undoc:<dir>:<symbol>` or `docs:pkg:<dir>`; the file and line are left out, so moving a declaration within its package keeps its issue. Severity is `low` and the group is the package directory. It only parses files: it never runs repository code and needs no network. It fails closed: a parse error, unreadable file, invalid path or more than 10,000 findings fails the run with nothing filed. A human-owned `exclude` file in the role directory skips package directories (`dir/` is a directory and everything below it, anything else a glob matched against the package directory); an entry makes its findings vanish, so autoclose closes their issues. Go only for now.\n54\t \n55\t Intervals and group sizes are starting values to tune, not measurements.\n56\t@@ -418,6 +421,7 @@ overrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n57\t   scanners/cve:             { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n58\t   scanners/docs:            { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n59\t   scanners/error-codes:     { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n60\t+  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n61\t   scanners/lint:            { every: 24h, max_open: 3, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n62\t   triage/lead:              { sidecar: vpe-specs, timeout: 15m, model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n63\t   triage/architect:         { sidecar: vpe-specs }\n64\t@@ -431,7 +435,7 @@ overrides:                   # only what differs from convention\n65\t \n66\t Scanners also take `route` (`pending`, `none` or `needs-human`). Anything unset takes its default: intake in `label` mode with `ard:pending`, scanners every 4 h with `max_open` 5 and `group_size` 10, triage every 15 min, a 30-minute job timeout, `make test`, 2 test-fix attempts, 3 review rounds and worker diff thresholds of 1,000 lines (warn) and 2,000 lines (hold). Durations accept `m`, `h` and `d`. A sidecar `repo` must be `owner/name` and its `ref` a valid git ref name (no `:`, leading `-`, `..` or spaces; an abbreviated SHA is rejected, use all 40 characters); `ard config check` reports the file and key. A worker's `timeout` and `max_budget_usd` cover the whole job (every step), and `tests: \"\"` disables its test step. Per-role keys are `every`, `max_open`, `group_size`, `autoclose`, `timeout`, `agent`, `model`, `max_budget_usd`, `budget_usd_per_day` (that role's own daily cap in USD; unset or 0 means only the repo cap applies), `sidecar`, `after`, `plan_section`, `tests`, `max_test_fixes`, `max_review_rounds`, `diff_warn_lines` and `diff_max_lines` (worker roles; positive integers, warn no more than max; above warn the PR proceeds with a note, above max it is held), `reviewers` and `when` (`paths`, or `triage` roles that ran; at least one is required). `ard config check` warns when every reviewer has a `when:` rule, because a PR matching none gets no review and stays a draft. `plan_section` is for triage roles: the `## <heading>` of `plan.md` the role owns (one line, no leading `#`, unique across triage roles). The starter roles default to Requirements (product-manager), Design (architect), UX (designer), Docs (documentation-planner) and Implementation (engineer), and a value in `config.yaml` overrides that; a triage role with none may write only its own role file. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\n67\t \n68\t-**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n69\t+**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `scanners/trufflehog`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n70\t \n71\t **Where `ard serve` reads config (decided, #87).** After each fetch into its own clone (`~/.ard/repos/<owner>/<repo>.git`, see Local-executor details) `ard serve` resolves `origin/main` to a SHA and reads `config.yaml` and the role directories from that commit, not from the working tree. It exports them into a snapshot at `~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/<sha>/`, kept 24 hours after a newer SHA replaces it, because roles run from a host path: a role directory, its `Dockerfile` and the scan worktree must all describe the one commit the tick's jobs use. Editing the host's working tree therefore changes nothing on a running controller, with one exception: a local `paused: true` is honoured (see the kill switch), and only that key is read locally. A merged change applies on the next tick without a pull. Symlinks and submodules under the role directories are rejected, and a config that cannot be fetched or does not validate counts as paused. If `origin/main` cannot be loaded at startup, `ard serve` starts paused instead of exiting, posts the load error to the status issue once per distinct error, and retries every tick; no loop runs until a config has loaded. `ard config check` validates the working tree, for authoring; `ard config check --ref <ref>` validates a commit of the local checkout (for example `--ref origin/main` after `git fetch`) without fetching.\n72\t \n73\tdiff --git a/internal/initcmd/body.go b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n74\tindex b9fea42..6a5ccd0 100644\n75\t--- a/internal/initcmd/body.go\n76\t+++ b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n77\t@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ func initBody(ops []op, res *config.Resolved) string {\n78\t \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Before you merge\\n\\n\")\n79\t \tb.WriteString(\"- Nothing takes effect until this is merged: ard serve reads its configuration from origin/main.\\n\")\n80\t \tb.WriteString(\"- Merge with **Squash and merge** (recommended); **Create a merge commit** is also safe. Never fast-forward this branch into main from the command line: the bot-commit check reads main's first-parent history and would fail on the bot's commit.\\n\")\n81\t+\tb.WriteString(\"- `scanners/trufflehog` is included. It files leaked-credential issues for a human (never for an agent) and needs a TruffleHog binary (AGPL-3.0; it is installed by the role's Dockerfile or taken from the host, and is not in the ard image). To opt out, delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` and its `scanners/trufflehog` line under `overrides:` in `.ard/config.yaml` before merging.\\n\")\n82\t \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Follow-up the App cannot do\\n\\n\")\n83\t \tb.WriteString(\"ard's GitHub App has no permission to write `.github/`, so do this by hand:\\n\\n\")\n84\t \tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\n85\tdiff --git a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n86\tindex 09ee735..dccb5e8 100644\n87\t--- a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n88\t+++ b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n89\t@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ func snapshot(t *testing.T, dir string) map[string]string {\n90\t \treturn m\n91\t }\n92\t \n93\t-var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n94\t+var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n95\t \n96\t func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n97\t \th := newHarness(t)\n98\t@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n99\t \tif pr.HeadRef != \"ard-init\" || pr.BaseRef != \"main\" || pr.Draft {\n100\t \t\tt.Errorf(\"pr = %+v\", pr)\n101\t \t}\n102\t-\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n103\t+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/`\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n104\t \t\tif !strings.Contains(pr.Body, s) {\n105\t \t\t\tt.Errorf(\"PR body lacks %q:\\n%s\", s, pr.Body)\n106\t \t\t}\n107\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/config.yaml b/internal/roles/config.yaml\n108\tindex a72acd4..fc4954c 100644\n109\t--- a/internal/roles/config.yaml\n110\t+++ b/internal/roles/config.yaml\n111\t@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@ overrides:\n112\t   scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n113\t   scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n114\t   scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n115\t+  # Leaked credentials go straight to a human: route: needs-human files without\n116\t+  # ard:pending, so no agent triages them.\n117\t+  scanners/trufflehog: { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n118\t   triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n119\t   triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n120\t   # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n121\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/roles.go b/internal/roles/roles.go\n122\tindex 7f2526f..272d965 100644\n123\t--- a/internal/roles/roles.go\n124\t+++ b/internal/roles/roles.go\n125\t@@ -7,11 +7,11 @@ package roles\n126\t import \"embed\"\n127\t \n128\t // FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n129\t-// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n130\t+// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n131\t //\n132\t // scanners/missing-tests is left out until its scan driver exists; re-add it when wiring it in.\n133\t //\n134\t-//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes triage workers\n135\t+//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes scanners/trufflehog triage workers\n136\t var FS embed.FS\n137\t \n138\t // ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\n139\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/roles_test.go b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n140\tindex 84698ba..747cad1 100644\n141\t--- a/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n142\t+++ b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n143\t@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n144\t \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n145\t \t}\n146\t \tsort.Strings(got)\n147\t-\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n148\t+\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \"scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n149\t \tif strings.Join(got, \",\") != strings.Join(want, \",\") {\n150\t \t\tt.Fatalf(\"embedded files = %v, want %v\", got, want)\n151\t \t}\n152\t@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n153\t // embed.FS reports 0444 for everything, so the exec bit must be checked on disk\n154\t // to catch a mode lost in git.\n155\t func TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk(t *testing.T) {\n156\t-\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\"} {\n157\t+\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\"} {\n158\t \t\tfi, err := os.Stat(p)\n159\t \t\tif err != nil {\n160\t \t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n161\t@@ -168,3 +168,29 @@ func starterFS(t *testing.T, chmod bool) fstest.MapFS {\n162\t \t}\n163\t \treturn m\n164\t }\n165\t+\n166\t+func TestEmbeddedTrufflehogRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n167\t+\tres, err := config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, true), \"/repo\")\n168\t+\tif err != nil {\n169\t+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFS: %v\", err)\n170\t+\t}\n171\t+\tfor _, r := range res.Roles {\n172\t+\t\tif r.Kind != config.KindScanner || r.Name != \"trufflehog\" {\n173\t+\t\t\tcontinue\n174\t+\t\t}\n175\t+\t\tif r.ScanPath != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\" || !r.Autoclose || r.Every != 24*time.Hour || r.GroupSize != 1 || r.MaxOpen != 5 || r.Timeout != 30*time.Minute {\n176\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected role: %+v\", r)\n177\t+\t\t}\n178\t+\t\tif r.Route != config.RouteNeedsHuman {\n179\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Route = %v, want needs-human\", r.Route)\n180\t+\t\t}\n181\t+\t\tif r.Dockerfile != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\" {\n182\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Dockerfile = %q\", r.Dockerfile)\n183\t+\t\t}\n184\t+\t\tif !slices.Equal(r.Extra, []string{\"exclude-paths\", \"findings.jq\"}) {\n185\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Extra = %v, want [exclude-paths findings.jq]\", r.Extra)\n186\t+\t\t}\n187\t+\t\treturn\n188\t+\t}\n189\t+\tt.Fatal(\"no scanner role trufflehog\")\n190\t+}\n191\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\n192\tnew file mode 100644\n193\tindex 0000000..3d54fc7\n194\t--- /dev/null\n195\t+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\n196\t@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n197\t+# Pinned tool image for the trufflehog scanner. Versions verified 2026-11-23:\n198\t+#   trufflehog 3.100.0 (released 2026-11-19), jq 1.8.2.\n199\t+# The trufflehog tarball checksums come from trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt,\n200\t+# whose signature was verified on 2026-11-23 with cosign v3.1.4 (\"Verified OK\"):\n201\t+#   cosign verify-blob trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt \\\n202\t+#     --certificate trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.pem \\\n203\t+#     --signature trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.sig \\\n204\t+#     --certificate-identity-regexp 'https://github\\.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/' \\\n205\t+#     --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n206\t+# jq's checksums are the ones in scanners/cve/Dockerfile.\n207\t+# The base is the same golang:1.27.4-trixie index digest as cve and the ard\n208\t+# image (root Dockerfile), so the layers are shared.\n209\t+#\n210\t+# LICENCE: trufflehog is AGPL-3.0. It is downloaded into this role's image only;\n211\t+# the binary is NOT in the published ard image.\n212\t+#\n213\t+# The image does NOT copy `scan` or `findings.jq`: the executor mounts this role\n214\t+# directory read-only, so the mounted script is always the one that runs.\n215\t+# Run:  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/repo:ro -v <role dir>:/role:ro -w /repo IMAGE /role/scan\n216\t+\n217\t+ARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n218\t+\n219\t+FROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\n220\t+ARG TARGETARCH\n221\t+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=3.100.0\n222\t+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64=b2d85eba59865e98f45c9fc9f77d2c6d62df529fdd5755af121304ea5a7cecbb\n223\t+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64=aa61657049229ae523e8455fcbba87dff57b0a2ba6bdb391a38cf75e6d4016dd\n224\t+ARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\n225\t+ARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\n226\t+ARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\n227\t+RUN set -eu; \\\n228\t+    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n229\t+      amd64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n230\t+      arm64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n231\t+      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n232\t+    esac; \\\n233\t+    mkdir /out; \\\n234\t+    curl -fsSL -o /tmp/th.tgz \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_${TARGETARCH}.tar.gz\"; \\\n235\t+    echo \"${th_sha}  /tmp/th.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n236\t+    tar -xzf /tmp/th.tgz -C /out trufflehog; \\\n237\t+    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n238\t+    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n239\t+    chmod 0755 /out/trufflehog /out/jq\n240\t+\n241\t+FROM ${GO_IMAGE}\n242\t+COPY --from=tools /out/trufflehog /usr/local/bin/trufflehog\n243\t+COPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n244\t+# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs; keep the temp dir in /var/tmp.\n245\t+ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\n246\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\n247\tnew file mode 100644\n248\tindex 0000000..b83ab0b\n249\t--- /dev/null\n250\t+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\n251\t@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n252\t+# trufflehog path regexes (Go RE2), one per line, matched against repo-relative\n253\t+# paths. Human-owned: change it in a reviewed PR. scan drops # lines and blanks.\n254\t+# .ard/<n>/logs/ were secret-scanned at close-out (model signature blobs are noise).\n255\t+^\\.ard/[0-9]+/logs/\n256\t+^vendor/\n257\t+^node_modules/\n258\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\n259\tnew file mode 100644\n260\tindex 0000000..23ef8a6\n261\t--- /dev/null\n262\t+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\n263\t@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n264\t+# project: trufflehog --json result lines in; one \"<base64 secret>\\t<json>\" line out\n265\t+#          per result. The json holds only d (DetectorName), f (file), l (line).\n266\t+#          Errors carry fixed text only (scan drops this stage's stderr anyway).\n267\t+# merge:   \"<h16>\\t<json>\" lines in (-n -R, inputs); findings out.\n268\t+def die(m): error(\"trufflehog: \" + m);\n269\t+\n270\t+def project:\n271\t+  if type != \"object\" then die(\"result is not an object\") else . end\n272\t+  | (.SourceMetadata.Data.Filesystem // die(\"result has no filesystem location\")) as $fs\n273\t+  | (if (.Raw | type) == \"string\" and .Raw != \"\" then .Raw\n274\t+     elif (.RawV2 | type) == \"string\" and .RawV2 != \"\" then .RawV2\n275\t+     else die(\"result has no Raw or RawV2 value\") end) as $secret\n276\t+  | (.DetectorName | if type == \"string\" and test(\"^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$\") then . else die(\"bad detector name\") end) as $d\n277\t+  | ($fs.file | if type == \"string\" then ltrimstr(\"./\") else die(\"result file is not a string\") end) as $f\n278\t+  | if $f == \"\" or ($f | startswith(\"/\")) or ($f | split(\"/\") | any(. == \"..\" or . == \".\" or . == \"\"))\n279\t+       or ($f | explode | any(. < 32 or . == 127))\n280\t+    then die(\"result file is not a clean repo-relative path\") else . end\n281\t+  | ($fs.line // 0 | if type == \"number\" and . >= 0 then floor else die(\"bad line\") end) as $l\n282\t+  | \"\\($secret | @base64)\\t\\({d: $d, f: $f, l: $l} | tojson)\";\n283\t+\n284\t+# A code span whose fence is longer than any backtick run in the text.\n285\t+def code: ([match(\"`+\"; \"g\").length] | max // 0) as $n | (\"`\" * ($n + 1)) as $fence\n286\t+  | if $n > 0 then \"\\($fence) \\(.) \\($fence)\" else \"\\($fence)\\(.)\\($fence)\" end;\n287\t+\n288\t+def merge($allow):\n289\t+  [inputs | select(length > 0) | split(\"\\t\")\n290\t+   | if length != 2 or (.[0] | test(\"^[0-9a-f]{16}$\") | not) then die(\"bad hashed line\") else . end\n291\t+   | {h: .[0]} + (.[1] | fromjson)]\n292\t+  | map(select((\"trufflehog:\" + .h) as $fp | $allow | index($fp) | not))\n293\t+  | group_by(.h)\n294\t+  | map((\"trufflehog:\" + .[0].h) as $fp\n295\t+      | (map(.d) | unique) as $dets\n296\t+      | (map({f, l}) | unique_by([.f, .l]) | sort_by(.f, .l)) as $locs\n297\t+      | ($locs | map(.f) | unique) as $files\n298\t+      | {fingerprint: $fp,\n299\t+         title: (\"Possible \\($dets[0]) credential in \\($files[0])\" | .[0:200]),\n300\t+         severity: \"high\", group: \"\", files: $files[0:1000],\n301\t+         body: ([\n302\t+           \"trufflehog matched a value that looks like a credential (detector: \\($dets | map(code) | join(\", \"))). ard did not verify it and never stores or prints the value.\",\n303\t+           \"\",\n304\t+           \"**Treat it as leaked.** Revoke or rotate it at the provider first. Deleting the line does not revoke it: the value stays in git history, and on a public repository it is already public.\",\n305\t+           \"\",\n306\t+           \"**Do not add `ard:pending` to this issue before the credential is rotated.** Triage and worker agents would read the file that holds it.\",\n307\t+           \"\",\n308\t+           \"What to do: 1. Rotate or revoke the credential at the provider. 2. Remove the value from HEAD in a PR. The issue closes itself on the next run (within 24 hours) once the value is gone from HEAD; that means gone from HEAD, not rotated. 3. Do not close this issue as completed while the value is still at HEAD: the next run refiles it. 4. For a false positive or a test fixture, add the fingerprint to `allow` or the path to `exclude-paths` (a reviewed PR), or close as not planned (it refiles after 90 days). 5. At 5 open issues the scanner does not run, so close fixed ones by hand once the value is gone. 6. Git history is not scanned or rewritten; rotation is what makes that safe.\",\n309\t+           \"\",\n310\t+           \"Not a secret? A maintainer adds the fingerprint below to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/allow`, or a path pattern to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths`, in a reviewed PR. Inline `trufflehog:ignore` comments are not honoured.\",\n311\t+           \"\",\n312\t+           \"Fingerprint: `\\($fp)`\",\n313\t+           \"\",\n314\t+           \"Locations at the scanned commit (\\($locs | length)):\"]\n315\t+           + ($locs[0:50] | map(\"- \\(.f | code)\" + (if .l > 0 then \" line \\(.l)\" else \"\" end)))\n316\t+           + (if ($locs | length) > 50 then [\"- and \\(($locs | length) - 50) more\"] else [] end)\n317\t+           + (if ($files | length) > 1000 then [\"\", \"Only the first 1,000 of \\($files | length) files are listed.\"] else [] end)\n318\t+           | join(\"\\n\"))})\n319\t+  | sort_by(.fingerprint) | .[];\n320\t+\n321\t+if $stage == \"project\" then project\n322\t+elif $stage == \"merge\" then merge($allow | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"#.*$\"; \"\") | gsub(\"^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$\"; \"\")) | map(select(. != \"\")))\n323\t+else die(\"unknown stage\") end\n324\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan\n325\tnew file mode 100755\n326\tindex 0000000..2b35737\n327\t--- /dev/null\n328\t+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan\n329\t@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n330\t+#!/bin/sh\n331\t+# trufflehog scanner: files leaked-credential findings for a human.\n332\t+#\n333\t+# Contract: run from the repository root (cwd) on the current commit. Sibling\n334\t+# files (findings.jq, exclude-paths, allow) are found from this script's own\n335\t+# path. Writes only to a temp dir. Needs no token. stdout (JSON lines, one\n336\t+# finding each) is printed only at the very end. Exit 0 = ok, 1 = failed\n337\t+# (nothing on stdout), 2 = a required tool is missing.\n338\t+#\n339\t+# Owner rules: no verification (--no-verification: no credential is ever sent\n340\t+# to a provider); HEAD only (filesystem scan, no history); only DetectorName,\n341\t+# the file, the line and a hash of the secret leave the project stage: Raw,\n342\t+# RawV2, Redacted, SecretParts, ExtraData, StructuredData and the rest never\n343\t+# leave this script. The secret exists only in pipes: never in a file, argv,\n344\t+# stdout or stderr. --no-ignore-tag: inline trufflehog:ignore is not honoured.\n345\t+#\n346\t+# Human-owned files next to this script: exclude-paths (regexes) and allow\n347\t+# (one trufflehog:<16 hex> fingerprint per line, # comments). A bad allow\n348\t+# entry fails the run. .git is always excluded.\n349\t+#\n350\t+# Never pass --since-commit, --max-depth, --detector-timeout, --archive-timeout,\n351\t+# --filter-unverified, --filter-entropy or --results: a partial or\n352\t+# load-dependent result would make the pipeline autoclose live findings.\n353\t+# Never use set -x: it would print the secret.\n354\t+set -eu\n355\t+dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n356\t+die() { echo \"trufflehog: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\n357\t+need() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"trufflehog: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n358\t+need trufflehog\n359\t+need jq\n360\t+if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sha() { sha256sum; }\n361\t+elif command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sha() { shasum -a 256; }\n362\t+else echo \"trufflehog: sha256sum not found\" >&2; exit 2; fi\n363\t+\n364\t+tmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-trufflehog.XXXXXX\")\n365\t+trap 'rm -rf \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n366\t+trap 'exit 130' INT\n367\t+trap 'exit 143' TERM\n368\t+\n369\t+echo \"trufflehog: $(trufflehog --version 2>&1 | head -n 1 || true)\" >&2\n370\t+\n371\t+# Exclusions: .git always, then the human-owned file without comments or blanks.\n372\t+printf '%s\\n' '^\\.git(/|$)' > \"$tmp/exclude\"\n373\t+if [ -e \"$dir/exclude-paths\" ]; then\n374\t+  grep -v -e '^[[:space:]]*#' -e '^[[:space:]]*$' \"$dir/exclude-paths\" >> \"$tmp/exclude\" || true\n375\t+fi\n376\t+allow=$tmp/allow.txt\n377\t+: > \"$allow\"\n378\t+[ ! -e \"$dir/allow\" ] || cat \"$dir/allow\" > \"$allow\"\n379\t+jq -n -R --rawfile allow \"$allow\" '$allow | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"#.*$\"; \"\") | gsub(\"^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$\"; \"\"))\n380\t+  | map(select(. != \"\")) | if any(test(\"^trufflehog:[0-9a-f]{16}$\") | not) then error(\"bad\") else empty end' 2>/dev/null \\\n381\t+  || die \"allow: every entry must be trufflehog:<16 hex digits> (comments start with #)\"\n382\t+\n383\t+tab=$(printf '\\t')\n384\t+# The secret exists only in these pipes: never in a file, argv, stdout or stderr.\n385\t+# Each stage records its own status (no pipefail in POSIX sh); \"|| rc=$?\" keeps\n386\t+# set -e from skipping the echo.\n387\t+{\n388\t+  rc=0\n389\t+  trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification \\\n390\t+    --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2 -x \"$tmp/exclude\" \\\n391\t+    2>\"$tmp/th.err\" || rc=$?\n392\t+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/th.rc\"\n393\t+} | {\n394\t+  rc=0\n395\t+  # stderr dropped: a jq type error can quote the input, which holds the secret.\n396\t+  jq -r --arg stage project --arg allow \"\" -f \"$dir/findings.jq\" 2>/dev/null || rc=$?\n397\t+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/project.rc\"\n398\t+} | {\n399\t+  rc=0\n400\t+  while IFS=$tab read -r pre rest; do\n401\t+    h=$(printf 'ard-trufflehog-v1\\000%s' \"$pre\" | sha | cut -c1-16) || { rc=1; break; }\n402\t+    case $h in *[!0-9a-f]*|'') rc=1; break ;; esac\n403\t+    [ ${#h} -eq 16 ] || { rc=1; break; }\n404\t+    printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \"$h\" \"$rest\"\n405\t+  done\n406\t+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/hash.rc\"\n407\t+} > \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\"\n408\t+\n409\t+rcof() { [ -s \"$tmp/$1.rc\" ] && cat \"$tmp/$1.rc\" || echo missing; }\n410\t+th=$(rcof th)\n411\t+if [ \"$th\" != 0 ]; then\n412\t+  jq -r 'select(.level == \"error\") | \"trufflehog: \\(.msg // \"\") \\((.error // \"\") | tostring | .[0:200])\"' \\\n413\t+    \"$tmp/th.err\" 2>/dev/null | head -n 5 >&2 || true\n414\t+  die \"trufflehog failed (exit status $th)\"\n415\t+fi\n416\t+[ \"$(rcof project)\" = 0 ] || die \"cannot parse trufflehog results\"\n417\t+[ \"$(rcof hash)\" = 0 ] || die \"cannot hash a result\"\n418\t+\n419\t+summary=$(jq -c 'select(.msg == \"finished scanning\") | [.chunks, .verified_secrets, .unverified_secrets]' \\\n420\t+  \"$tmp/th.err\" 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1) || die \"cannot read trufflehog's log\"\n421\t+case $summary in\n422\t+  \\[[0-9]*,[0-9]*,[0-9]*\\]) ;;\n423\t+  *) die \"no \\\"finished scanning\\\" summary from trufflehog\" ;;\n424\t+esac\n425\t+set -- $(echo \"$summary\" | tr -d '[]' | tr ',' ' ')\n426\t+chunks=$1 want=$(($2 + $3))\n427\t+got=$(wc -l < \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\" | tr -d ' ')\n428\t+echo \"trufflehog: $chunks chunk(s), $got result(s)\" >&2\n429\t+if [ \"$chunks\" -eq 0 ] && [ -n \"$(find . -name .git -prune -o -type f -print | head -n 1)\" ]; then\n430\t+  die \"trufflehog scanned nothing in a non-empty tree (or every file is excluded)\"\n431\t+fi\n432\t+[ \"$got\" -eq \"$want\" ] || die \"result count $got does not match the summary's $want\"\n433\t+\n434\t+jq -n -R -c --arg stage merge --rawfile allow \"$allow\" -f \"$dir/findings.jq\" \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\" \\\n435\t+  > \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" || die \"merge failed\"\n436\t+echo \"trufflehog: $(wc -l < \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" | tr -d ' ') finding(s)\" >&2\n437\t+cat \"$tmp/out.jsonl\"\n438\tdiff --git a/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go b/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go\n439\tnew file mode 100644\n440\tindex 0000000..59d6f29\n441\t--- /dev/null\n442\t+++ b/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go\n443\t@@ -0,0 +1,292 @@\n444\t+package roles\n445\t+\n446\t+import (\n447\t+\t\"bytes\"\n448\t+\t\"encoding/json\"\n449\t+\t\"os\"\n450\t+\t\"os/exec\"\n451\t+\t\"path/filepath\"\n452\t+\t\"strings\"\n453\t+\t\"testing\"\n454\t+\n455\t+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/scanner\"\n456\t+)\n457\t+\n458\t+// thFake stands in for trufflehog: it records argv and replays stdout, stderr\n459\t+// and the exit code from files named by the environment.\n460\t+const thFake = `#!/bin/sh\n461\t+if [ \"${1:-}\" = --version ]; then echo \"trufflehog 3.100.0\"; exit 0; fi\n462\t+printf '%s\\n' \"$*\" >> \"$TH_ARGV\"\n463\t+[ -z \"${TH_STDOUT:-}\" ] || cat \"$TH_STDOUT\"\n464\t+[ -z \"${TH_STDERR:-}\" ] || cat \"$TH_STDERR\" >&2\n465\t+exit \"${TH_RC:-0}\"\n466\t+`\n467\t+\n468\t+type thResult struct {\n469\t+\tstdout, stderr string\n470\t+\tcode           int\n471\t+\targv           string\n472\t+\ttmp            string\n473\t+}\n474\t+\n475\t+type thLine map[string]any\n476\t+\n477\t+func thResultLine(raw, det, file string, line int) thLine {\n478\t+\treturn thLine{\"DetectorName\": det, \"Raw\": raw, \"RawV2\": \"v2-marker\", \"Redacted\": \"redacted-marker\",\n479\t+\t\t\"SourceMetadata\": map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Filesystem\": map[string]any{\"file\": file, \"line\": line}}}}\n480\t+}\n481\t+\n482\t+func thSummary(chunks, unverified int) string {\n483\t+\tb, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\"level\": \"info\", \"msg\": \"finished scanning\", \"chunks\": chunks, \"verified_secrets\": 0, \"unverified_secrets\": unverified})\n484\t+\treturn string(b)\n485\t+}\n486\t+\n487\t+func thJoin(lines []thLine) string {\n488\t+\tvar sb strings.Builder\n489\t+\tfor _, l := range lines {\n490\t+\t\tb, _ := json.Marshal(l)\n491\t+\t\tsb.Write(b)\n492\t+\t\tsb.WriteByte('\\n')\n493\t+\t}\n494\t+\treturn sb.String()\n495\t+}\n496\t+\n497\t+// thRun runs the shipped scan in a temp repo with a fake trufflehog.\n498\t+func thRun(t *testing.T, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n499\t+\tt.Helper()\n500\t+\treturn thRunFull(t, mustAbs(t, \"scanners/trufflehog\"), out, errlog, rc, files, extra)\n501\t+}\n502\t+\n503\t+func thRunWith(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n504\t+\tt.Helper()\n505\t+\treturn thRunFull(t, role, out, errlog, rc, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n506\t+}\n507\t+\n508\t+func thRunFull(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n509\t+\tt.Helper()\n510\t+\tneedTools(t, \"sh\", \"jq\")\n511\t+\tif _, err := exec.LookPath(\"sha256sum\"); err != nil {\n512\t+\t\tneedTools(t, \"shasum\")\n513\t+\t}\n514\t+\twork := t.TempDir()\n515\t+\trepo := filepath.Join(work, \"repo\")\n516\t+\tbin := filepath.Join(work, \"bin\")\n517\t+\ttmp := filepath.Join(work, \"tmp\")\n518\t+\tfor _, d := range []string{repo, bin, tmp} {\n519\t+\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(d, 0o755); err != nil {\n520\t+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n521\t+\t\t}\n522\t+\t}\n523\t+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(bin, \"trufflehog\"), []byte(thFake), 0o755); err != nil {\n524\t+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n525\t+\t}\n526\t+\tfor name, body := range files {\n527\t+\t\tp := filepath.Join(repo, name)\n528\t+\t\tos.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(p), 0o755)\n529\t+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(p, []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n530\t+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n531\t+\t\t}\n532\t+\t}\n533\t+\tfor name, body := range map[string]string{\"stdout\": out, \"stderr\": errlog} {\n534\t+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(work, name), []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n535\t+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n536\t+\t\t}\n537\t+\t}\n538\t+\tcmd := exec.Command(\"sh\", filepath.Join(role, \"scan\"))\n539\t+\tcmd.Dir = repo\n540\t+\tcmd.Env = []string{\"PATH=\" + bin + \":\" + os.Getenv(\"PATH\"), \"TMPDIR=\" + tmp, \"TH_ARGV=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"argv\"),\n541\t+\t\t\"TH_STDOUT=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"stdout\"), \"TH_STDERR=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"stderr\"), \"TH_RC=\" + string(rune('0'+rc))}\n542\t+\tfor k, v := range extra {\n543\t+\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, k+\"=\"+v)\n544\t+\t}\n545\t+\tvar so, se bytes.Buffer\n546\t+\tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = &so, &se\n547\t+\tcode := 0\n548\t+\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n549\t+\t\tee, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError)\n550\t+\t\tif !ok {\n551\t+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n552\t+\t\t}\n553\t+\t\tcode = ee.ExitCode()\n554\t+\t}\n555\t+\targv, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(work, \"argv\"))\n556\t+\treturn thResult{so.String(), se.String(), code, string(argv), tmp}\n557\t+}\n558\t+\n559\t+func thTmpEmpty(t *testing.T, tmp string) {\n560\t+\tt.Helper()\n561\t+\tif ents, _ := os.ReadDir(tmp); len(ents) != 0 {\n562\t+\t\tt.Errorf(\"temp dir not cleaned: %v\", ents)\n563\t+\t}\n564\t+}\n565\t+\n566\t+func TestTrufflehogAggregatesAndFingerprints(t *testing.T) {\n567\t+\tin := thJoin([]thLine{\n568\t+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Zeta\", \"sub/b.txt\", 3),\n569\t+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1),\n570\t+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"./a.txt\", 1),\n571\t+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-beta\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 2),\n572\t+\t})\n573\t+\tr := thRun(t, in, thSummary(2, 4), 0, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n574\t+\tif r.code != 0 {\n575\t+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit %d: %s\", r.code, r.stderr)\n576\t+\t}\n577\t+\tfs, err := scanner.DecodeFindings(strings.NewReader(r.stdout))\n578\t+\tif err != nil {\n579\t+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n580\t+\t}\n581\t+\tif len(fs) != 2 {\n582\t+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"findings = %d, want 2:\\n%s\", len(fs), r.stdout)\n583\t+\t}\n584\t+\tgot := map[string]scanner.Finding{}\n585\t+\tfor _, f := range fs {\n586\t+\t\tgot[f.Fingerprint] = f\n587\t+\t}\n588\t+\talpha, ok := got[\"trufflehog:d4bf4d1967fad7b7\"]\n589\t+\tif !ok || got[\"trufflehog:ce658c895bb3b307\"].Fingerprint == \"\" {\n590\t+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"golden fingerprints missing:\\n%s\", r.stdout)\n591\t+\t}\n592\t+\tif alpha.Title != \"Possible Alpha credential in a.txt\" || alpha.Severity != \"high\" || strings.Join(alpha.Files, \",\") != \"a.txt,sub/b.txt\" {\n593\t+\t\tt.Errorf(\"alpha = %+v\", alpha)\n594\t+\t}\n595\t+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"Do not add `ard:pending`\", \"1. Rotate\", \"6. Git history\"} {\n596\t+\t\tif !strings.Contains(alpha.Body, s) {\n597\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"body lacks %q\", s)\n598\t+\t\t}\n599\t+\t}\n600\t+\tfor _, leak := range []string{\"canary-raw\", \"v2-marker\", \"redacted-marker\"} {\n601\t+\t\tif strings.Contains(r.stdout+r.stderr, leak) {\n602\t+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%q leaked\", leak)\n603\t+\t\t}\n604\t+\t}\n605\t+\tthTmpEmpty(t, r.tmp)\n606\t+\t// deterministic: reversed input gives identical stdout\n607\t+\tlines := strings.Split(strings.TrimSpace(in), \"\\n\")\n608\t+\tfor i, j := 0, len(lines)-1; i < j; i, j = i+1, j-1 {\n609\t+\t\tlines[i], lines[j] = lines[j], lines[i]\n610\t+\t}\n611\t+\tr2 := thRun(t, strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")+\"\\n\", thSummary(2, 4), 0, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n612\t+\tif r2.stdout != r.stdout {\n613\t+\t\tt.Errorf(\"output depends on input order\")\n614\t+\t}\n615\t+}\n616\t+\n617\t+func TestTrufflehogFailsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n618\t+\tok := thResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1)\n619\t+\tbad := func(mut func(thLine)) string {\n620\t+\t\tl := thResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1)\n621\t+\t\tmut(l)\n622\t+\t\treturn thJoin([]thLine{l})\n623\t+\t}\n624\t+\tfsData := func(l thLine, file any) {\n625\t+\t\tl[\"SourceMetadata\"] = map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Filesystem\": map[string]any{\"file\": file}}}\n626\t+\t}\n627\t+\tcases := []struct {\n628\t+\t\tname, out, log string\n629\t+\t\trc             int\n630\t+\t\tallow          string\n631\t+\t\twant           string\n632\t+\t}{\n633\t+\t\t{\"exit1\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 1, \"\", \"failed (exit status 1)\"},\n634\t+\t\t{\"exit2\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 2, \"\", \"failed (exit status 2)\"},\n635\t+\t\t{\"no summary\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), \"\", 0, \"\", \"finished scanning\"},\n636\t+\t\t{\"zero chunks\", \"\", thSummary(0, 0), 0, \"\", \"scanned nothing\"},\n637\t+\t\t{\"count mismatch\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 2), 0, \"\", \"does not match\"},\n638\t+\t\t{\"malformed\", \"{not json\\n\", thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n639\t+\t\t{\"non-object\", \"[1]\\n\", thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n640\t+\t\t{\"absolute path\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"/etc/x\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n641\t+\t\t{\"dotdot\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"../x\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n642\t+\t\t{\"inner dotdot\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"a/../b\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n643\t+\t\t{\"control char\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"a\\nb\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n644\t+\t\t{\"git source\", bad(func(l thLine) { l[\"SourceMetadata\"] = map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Git\": map[string]any{}}} }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n645\t+\t\t{\"no raw\", bad(func(l thLine) { delete(l, \"Raw\"); delete(l, \"RawV2\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n646\t+\t\t{\"bad detector\", bad(func(l thLine) { l[\"DetectorName\"] = \"bad name!\" }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n647\t+\t\t{\"bad allow\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"nonsense\\n\", \"allow:\"},\n648\t+\t}\n649\t+\tfor _, c := range cases {\n650\t+\t\tt.Run(c.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n651\t+\t\t\tneedTools(t, \"sh\", \"jq\")\n652\t+\t\t\trole := mustAbs(t, \"scanners/trufflehog\")\n653\t+\t\t\tif c.allow != \"\" { // allow lives beside scan: use a copy of the role dir\n654\t+\t\t\t\tcp := t.TempDir()\n655\t+\t\t\t\tfor _, n := range []string{\"scan\", \"findings.jq\", \"exclude-paths\"} {\n656\t+\t\t\t\t\tb, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(role, n))\n657\t+\t\t\t\t\tos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(cp, n), b, 0o755)\n658\t+\t\t\t\t}\n659\t+\t\t\t\tos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(cp, \"allow\"), []byte(c.allow), 0o644)\n660\t+\t\t\t\trole = cp\n661\t+\t\t\t}\n662\t+\t\t\tr := thRunRole(t, role, c.out, c.log, c.rc)\n663\t+\t\t\tif r.code == 0 || r.stdout != \"\" {\n664\t+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit %d, stdout %q; want failure with empty stdout\", r.code, r.stdout)\n665\t+\t\t\t}\n666\t+\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(r.stderr, c.want) {\n667\t+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr lacks %q:\\n%s\", c.want, r.stderr)\n668\t+\t\t\t}\n669\t+\t\t\tif strings.Contains(r.stderr, \"canary-raw\") {\n670\t+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr leaks the secret:\\n%s\", r.stderr)\n671\t+\t\t\t}\n672\t+\t\t\tthTmpEmpty(t, r.tmp)\n673\t+\t\t})\n674\t+\t}\n675\t+}\n676\t+\n677\t+// thRunRole is thRun against another role directory (used for allow files).\n678\t+func thRunRole(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n679\t+\tt.Helper()\n680\t+\treturn thRunWith(t, role, out, errlog, rc)\n681\t+}\n682\t+\n683\t+func TestTrufflehogArgvAndExcludes(t *testing.T) {\n684\t+\tr := thRun(t, \"\", thSummary(0, 0), 0, nil, nil)\n685\t+\tif r.code != 0 || r.stdout != \"\" {\n686\t+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"empty repo: exit %d stdout %q stderr %s\", r.code, r.stdout, r.stderr)\n687\t+\t}\n688\t+\targv := strings.TrimSpace(r.argv)\n689\t+\tif !strings.HasPrefix(argv, \"filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2 -x \") {\n690\t+\t\tt.Errorf(\"argv = %q\", argv)\n691\t+\t}\n692\t+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"--since-commit\", \"--max-depth\", \"--detector-timeout\", \"--arch